": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Switch Case in JavaScript", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about switch statements.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modal Verbs for Speculating: May and Could", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are <strong>modal verbs</strong> used to speculate about something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <b>modal verbs</b> to express obligation, possibility, certainty and speculation, among others. In this learning point, we are going to talk about the modal verbs \u2018<b>may</b>' and \u2018<b>could</b>' that can be used to speculate or express an assumption about a given situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When we want to perform a multiway branch, we may want to use switch statements. This could simplify the decision making process.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you think that knowing the syntax may help understand how switch statements work more easily?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think this process may be difficult. There are many conditions to take into account.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We use <b>could</b> to indicate that a situation or result is highly probable. On the other hand, <b>may</b> is used to express that a situation or result is slightly possible.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: </br><i>You <b>could </b> use conditional statements in Javascript to help your program make correct decisions.</br> You <b>may</b> use the \u2018if\u2026else\u2026if' statement instead of the \u2018if\u2026else' one for this specific situation. But you'd better double check with the manager.  </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Finally, remember that we can use <b>modal verbs</b> in different tenses and forms depending on what we want to express. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:</br><i> This code <b>may have been written</b> by the software development team.  </br><b>Could</b> we use switch statements in Javascript? </br>He <b>may not</b> have been ready for this company. I think that's why he quitted. </i>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Flowchart of How a Switch Statement Works", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Switch statements</strong> integrate multiple \u201cif\u2026else\u2026if\u201d statements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we have different conditions, we can use multiple \u2018if\u2026else .. if' statements for performing a multiway branch, Nevertheless, we can also use switch statements to accomplish the same goal in a more efficient way, especially if all the branches depend on the value of one variable. Let's take a look at the following flowchart:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07img01.jpg", "type": "image"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "multiway ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having different possibilities or paths to take", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When we want to perform a multiway branch, we may want to use switch statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "branch ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a part or section of a structure  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When we want to perform a multiway branch, we may want to use switch statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "execute a condition ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to choose and process a given condition to carry out a specific function in a program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If the interpreter goes over all the cases and finds no match, the default condition will be executed.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "match", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to correspond or have compatible characteristics with a different element", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Once you've done this, you'll to write a default statement that will be executed if none of the previous conditions matched.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "default", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a value that the program assumes when no other values were specified  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If the interpreter goes over all the cases and finds no match, the default condition will be executed.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for more information about Switch Statements in JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a chart with examples comparing Switch Stamens and \u201cif\u2026 else\u2026 if\u201d statements.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Prepare a poster including what Switch statements are and an example. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the poster with the class. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I use switch statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify information in a flowchart of a switch statement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I understand the syntax for a switch statement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}]}